# Frontend standards (MyWallet)

Vue 3 + Inertia lives under `resources/js/`. **TypeScript only** (`strict: true`). No new plain `.js`.

## TDD first

1. Failing Vitest unit/component test under `tests/Frontend/`.
2. Minimal implementation.
3. Keep green.

## Architecture (inward only)

```
Pages / Components / Layouts (presentation)
        ↓
   application/     (use cases — rare; Inertia server owns most flows)
        ↓
   domain/          (pure types, formatters, enums — no Vue, no fetch)
infrastructure/     (axios bootstrap, localStorage theme, Ziggy helpers)
```

| Path | Responsibility |
|------|----------------|
| `domain/` | Money/date formatters, wallet/TX type maps — pure functions |
| `application/` | Client use cases only when logic is not “just Inertia form” |
| `infrastructure/` | HTTP bootstrap, theme storage, browser APIs |
| `Pages/`, `Components/`, `Layouts/`, `Composables/` | Presentation — props in, callbacks out |
| `types/` | Shared Inertia page prop types |

Alias `@` → `resources/js`.

Pages compose UI + Inertia `useForm` / `router`. Do not put parse/format business rules in SFCs — import from `domain/`.

**Incremental typing:** all SFCs use `<script setup lang="ts">`. Shared layers (`domain/`, `infrastructure/`, `Components/`, `Layouts/`, `Pages/Auth/Login.vue`) are covered by `npm run typecheck`. Remaining Pages still use runtime `defineProps`; tighten with typed props when touching a page (`npm run typecheck:all`).

## TypeScript

- `strict: true`, prefer `noUncheckedIndexedAccess`.
- **No `any` / `as any`**. Boundary data: `unknown` → typed props/entities.
- Explicit return types on exported domain/application functions.
- Vue SFCs: `<script setup lang="ts">`.

## OAuth / external redirects

Never use Inertia `<Link>` or `router.visit` for Google (or any cross-origin OAuth). Use a normal `<a href="...">` full-page navigation.

## Testing (Vitest)

| Target | Location |
|--------|----------|
| Domain pure logic | `tests/Frontend/domain/...` |
| Components | `tests/Frontend/presentation/...` |

Mirror `resources/js/` relative paths under `tests/Frontend/`.

## Forbidden

- Business format/parse logic only inside Vue templates/scripts when it belongs in `domain/`
- `any`, disabling strict
- Domain importing Vue / Inertia / axios
- Inertia XHR to OAuth authorize URLs
